{"name":"Orange Salmonberry","hex":"#f0b073","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"},{"term":"salmonberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bush, Rubus spectabilis, found on the Pacific coast of North America.","The fruit from this bush, similar in appearance and texture to the blackberry and raspberry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salmonberry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rubus spectabilis","blocks":[{"text":"Rubus spectabilis, the salmonberry, is a species of bramble native to the west coast of North America. Its fruit is typically yellow-orange or red, resembling raspberries. The plant grows in the wild, and is not cultivated."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Salmonberry_%287303689554%29.jpg/330px-Salmonberry_%287303689554%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rubus_spectabilis","wikidata":"Q158361"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-D